    <exercise number="5" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Given $$f(x) = x^{2} + 2x$$ and $$g(x) = 6 - x^{2},$$ find $$f + g, f - g, fg,$$ and $$\frac{f}{g}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$(f+g)( x )=2x+6, (f+g)( x )=2x+6,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,\infty ) (-\infty ,\infty )$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$(f-g)( x )=2 x 2 +2x-6, (f-g)( x )=2 x 2 +2x-6,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,\infty ) (-\infty ,\infty )$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$(fg)( x )=- x 4 -2 x 3 +6 x 2 +12x, (fg)( x )=- x 4 -2 x 3 +6 x 2 +12x,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,\infty ) (-\infty ,\infty )$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$( f g )( x )= x 2 +2x 6- x 2 , ( f g )( x )= x 2 +2x 6- x 2 ,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,- 6 )\cup (- 6 , 6 )\cup ( 6 ,\infty ) (-\infty ,- 6 )\cup (- 6 , 6 )\cup ( 6 ,\infty )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
