    <exercise number="7" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Given $$f(x) = 2x^{2} + 4x$$ and $$g(x) = \frac{1}{2x},$$ find $$f + g, f - g, fg,$$ and $$\frac{f}{g}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$(f+g)( x )= 4 x 3 +8 x 2 +1 2x , (f+g)( x )= 4 x 3 +8 x 2 +1 2x ,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty ) (-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty )$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$(f-g)( x )= 4 x 3 +8 x 2 -1 2x , (f-g)( x )= 4 x 3 +8 x 2 -1 2x ,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty ) (-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty )$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$(fg)( x )=x+2, (fg)( x )=x+2,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty ) (-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty )$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$( f g )( x )=4 x 3 +8 x 2 , ( f g )( x )=4 x 3 +8 x 2 ,$$ domain: $$(-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty ) (-\infty ,0)\cup (0,\infty )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
