    <exercise number="93" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>A rain drop hitting a lake makes a circular ripple. If the radius, in inches, grows as a function of time in minutes according to $$r(t) = 25\sqrt{t + 2},$$ find the area of the ripple as a function of time. Find the area of the ripple at $$t = 2.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$A(t)=\pi ( 25 t+2 ) 2 A(t)=\pi ( 25 t+2 ) 2$$ and $$A(2)=\pi ( 25 4 ) 2 =2500\pi A(2)=\pi ( 25 4 ) 2 =2500\pi$$ square inches</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
