        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐFind the composite function $$r\left( {V(t)} \right).$$</item>
          <item>ⓑFind the exact time when the radius reaches 10 inches.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="97" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The number of bacteria in a refrigerated food product is given by $$N(T) = 23T^{2} - 56T + 1,$$ $$3 &lt; T &lt; 33,$$ where $$T$$ is the temperature of the food. When the food is removed from the refrigerator, the temperature is given by $$T(t) = 5t + 1.5,$$ where $$t$$ is the time in hours.</paragraph>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐFind the composite function $$N\left( {T(t)} \right).$$</item>
          <item>ⓑFind the time (round to two decimal places) when the bacteria count reaches 6752.</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ $$N(T(t))=23 (5t+1.5) 2 -56(5t+1.5)+1 N(T(t))=23 (5t+1.5) 2 -56(5t+1.5)+1$$</item>
          <item>ⓑ 3.38 hours</item>
        </list>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
